# Agent authorizations as code — see docs/architecture/agents-authz.md.
#
# Any change to who/what an agent may do needs approval from a code owner who is NOT
# the author (branch protection: 1 approval, code-owner review required, last push
# approved by someone else, no bypass). Agents and bots are never code owners, so an
# agent-authored PR can never be approved by an agent.
#
# The rules and the drift job are owned too: weakening a rule must be as visible as
# weakening the file.
#
# TODO(before merge): add Denis's GitHub login to every line below, e.g.
#   /config/agents-authz.json  @phumblot-gs @<denis-login>
# Until then a PR authored by Pierre cannot be approved by a code owner.
/config/agents-authz.json                    @phumblot-gs
/packages/core/src/agents-authz*.ts          @phumblot-gs
/packages/core/src/__fixtures__/agents-authz/ @phumblot-gs
/packages/authz-drift-plugin/                @phumblot-gs
/scripts/check-agents-authz.ts               @phumblot-gs
/.github/workflows/agents-authz-changed.yml  @phumblot-gs
/.github/CODEOWNERS                          @phumblot-gs
